From 7e98221f806a3b05af8c1e4ac41c39c8dc4b791e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:34:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: Rakkashin: port the remaining Rakkashin Kernel
 optimizations to 7.3

From Goubata/Rakkashin-Kernel (android16-6.12, 7e0d0a6), features that were not
in the 7.3 port yet (the feature modules avr_profile, launch boost, thread
boost, Encore FAS, Boeffla, PELT multiplier, ADIOS and ntsync already were):

- Sultan: rcu_gp workqueue unbound; freezer timeout 1 s; no allocation for
  small kernfs writes (on-stack buffer) and for the SELinux inode context
  lookup (on-stack INITCONTEXTLEN buffer).
- LawRun: devfreq_wq high priority/unbound; page_cluster 0 (zram, no swap
  readahead); vfs_cache_pressure 50; watermark_boost_factor 0.
- NGK/AGNi: vmstat interval 20 s; binder debug_mask 0; dynamic fsync
  (/sys/module/sync/parameters/fsync_enabled); no warn_alloc() for OOM victims.
- avr: watermark_scale_factor 50; dirty writeback 15 s; tcp_notsent_lowat
  128K; tcp_slow_start_after_idle 0; -mtune=oryon-1 (tuning only, no ISA change).
- LZ4 1.9.x fast decompression loop (lib/lz4, as in Rakkashin), with the
  compressors moved to LZ4_wildCopy8.

The sched/idle single-state shortcut, tick dependency tracepoint check and
ratelimited capacity-change message are already native in 7.3.
Phone: all values verified at runtime on the 7.3 final boot.
